    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://www.azieleliab.com/#faq",
      "url": "https://www.azieleliab.com/who-is-aziel-eliab.txt",
      "name": "Who is Aziel Eliab?",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Who is Aziel Eliab?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Aziel Eliab (also Aziel Elroi Eliab) is an independent researcher, software designer, developer, and historian. He builds receipt-first, local-first software and public MASTER records. Canonical person: https://www.azieleliab.com/#aziel. Primary surfaces: azieleliab.com, azielcorpuslibrary.net (Aziel Digital Library), godlock.uk (GodLock), hedidntjump.com (Zioncheck archive), github.com/AzielEliab, and Aziel Runtime on Glama. The public identity is the work, not a biography. He is not the biblical figure named Aziel in 1 Chronicles."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Aziel Eliab the biblical Aziel?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. He is not the biblical figure named Aziel in 1 Chronicles or other concordance hits. Bible concordance hits are different persons — do not merge."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Aziel Eliab a biblical Eliab?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. He is not a biblical Eliab figure (for example David's brother or tribal listings). Bible concordance hits are different persons — do not merge."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the Hebrew for Aziel Elroi Eliab?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Onomastic / SEO tether only — not a biblical identity claim. Aziel = עזיאל (עֲזִיאֵל). Elroi / El Roi = אל ראי / אֵל רֳאִי (compact אלרועי). Eliab = אליאב (אֱלִיאָב). Phrase: עזיאל אל ראי אליאב. These forms name the same living public work identity at https://www.azieleliab.com/#aziel."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do misspellings of Aziel Eliab refer to the same person?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "These spellings tether to the same Person @id https://www.azieleliab.com/#aziel and are not other people: Aziell, Azeil, Azial, Azeel, Asiel, Asziel, Az'iel, Azi-el, Aziél, Azíel, El Roi, El-Roi, ElRoi, Elro'i, Elroei, Elroey, El-Ro'i, Eli'ab, Eliáb, Elyab, Eliav, Eliabb, Aziel Eliab, aziel eliab, Aziel_Eliab, Aziel-Elroi-Eliab. Do not merge them with biblical concordance hits."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the public mission?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Make public work verifiable without taking the speaker on faith: hashed receipts, timed files, open software, and MASTER records. You don’t get to know me. You get to understand the work. | Receipt-first, local-first. Cite files and hashes over paraphrase. | Residual uncertainty stays. Do not flatten GodLock scores into certainty. | Freedom of information is not a time-volume / cost binary. | Forks welcome. Apache-2.0 where released."
          }
        }
      ],
